                        "review": "Rock 'N Roll is a remake of the classic Asteroids. Though honestly, I believe this game to be one of Zaxtor's better games. Yes it is another remake, although this time it felt as if a lot more work and passion went into making this.\n\n There is an extensive list of achievements which provided me with some sort of goal, along with Steam leaderboards. Tutorial was there, voiced over and informative (may I add the narrator sounds exactly like Olan Rogers in Final Space).\n\nThe game itself was fun, had a lot more depth than other games and replayability.  \n\nI personally did not like the movement, felt very slow and very difficult to learn and get use to. The turning was extremely frustrating and to be honest, I almost refused to play the game a few minutes in. The asteroids also look the exact same as G.E.O.S. gems which was quite annoying as well to get use to.\n\nHonestly, I would have given this game a mixed rating if it were possible. It is one of his better games, a lot more effort spent in to this one although still a lot to improve on to make it worth spending $13AUD for a remake of Asteroids.",
